riod elapses without change and the reader raises RefineError::InvalidInput, which propagates as the workflow failure.\r\n\r\n  Why the agent produces malformed JSON here\r\n\r\n  The completion-contract prompt for plan/criticize/revise (codec.rs:290+) asks the agent to write one inline JSON object whose planning_result field is a nested object with\r\n  a summary string and a checklist array of {id, description} items. In practice:\r\n\r\n  - Model produces long, multi-sentence summary / description values �� occasionally forgets to close a bracket at the tail (all 6 EOF failures land in the ~2.3�V3.0 KB range\r\n  where the closing braces would be).\r\n  - Model occasionally writes a raw newline inside a string in summary �� JSON parser hits the \\u0000-\\u001F guard.\r\n  - The prompt gives one long inline JSON example; there is no post-write validation step.\r\n\r\n  Nothing tells the agent it wrote invalid JSON. Nothing gives it a chance to correct it. Refine sees the malformed file, waits 2s, gives up.\r\n\r\n  Requested fix (in rough priority order)\r\n\r\n  1. Retry loop instead of hard-fail. On InvalidInput from SignalReader::take, don't kill the round. Feed the parse error back to the agent through the existing command\r\n  channel with a short \"your signal.json did not parse: <error> �X rewrite it, keeping the same shape\" prompt, and re-poll. Cap at N (e.g., 3) attempts before failing. This\r\n  alone would recover the majority of these failures.\r\n  2. Require atomic write in the contract. Change the completion-contract prompt to instruct the agent to write to signal.json.tmp then mv into place. Then SignalReader can\r\n  treat \"file exists\" as \"fully written\" and drop the fingerprint-grace hack �X a parse failure becomes immediately actionable (feeds into fix #1).\r\n  3. Shrink the wire format. The failure mode is \"long nested JSON written inline.\" Two lower-risk shapes:\r\n    - Split it: signal.json carries only {\"state\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}; planning_result.json (or implementation_evidence.json) is a separate artifact. A malformed\r\n  planning_result no longer nukes the state signal.\r\n    - Or accept JSONL: one top-level JSON value per line, so a truncated final line is skippable.\r\n  4. Preserve the bad bytes for diagnosis. Today, on InvalidInput, cleanup_session_artifacts removes the signal file (session_runtime.rs:210+). Copy it to\r\n  <process_id>.signal.invalid.json first so we can see what the agent actually wrote. Right now we're guessing from column offsets because the evidence is deleted.\r\n  5. Model-side self-check in the prompt. Add a line to the completion contract along the lines of \"after writing, verify the file parses (e.g., jq . <path>), and rewrite if\r\n  it does not.\" Cheap and stacks with the other fixes.\r\n\r\n  Repro / evidence pointers\r\n\r\n  - Grace-period source: src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs:199�V254, agent_sessions.rs:24\r\n  - Prompt template that shapes the output: src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs:290�V (completion_contract)\r\n  - Recent operation files with the error: run/8082/operations/1a00549*, 1a005b87*, 1a005c81*, 1a005c85*, 1a005ca9*, 1a005d3b*, 1a005e40*\r\n  - Cleanup that deletes the offending bytes: src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs:265�V273, called from session_runtime.rs:210, 224, 236\r\n\r\n\r\n[cid:insurity-small2_2f81c33c-d951-4e5c-a467-1113541ca22c.jpg]\r\nBuddy Williams\r\nBuddy.Williams@insurity.com\r\n\r\n[cid:excellence2026signature(17b0688e-5473-4b74-96eb-a73f633f2c2f)_48407359-d77b-4967-95cd-277a32b50ebc.png]<https://insurity.com/excellence?utm_source=Email-Signature&utm_medium=Email&utm_campaign=Event-Excellence-2026>\r\n\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe information contained in this e-mail message is intended only for the personal and confidential use of the intended recipient(s). This message may be an attorney-client communication and/or work product and as such is privileged and confidential. If the reader of this message is not the intended recipient or an agent responsible for delivering it to the intended recipient, you are hereby notified that you have received this document in error and that any review, dissemination, distribution, or copying of this message is strictly prohibited. If you have received this communication in error, please notify us immediately by e-mail, and delete the original message.\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n~~~Insurity~~~",
