      "prompt": "From: Buddy Williams <buddy.williams@insurity.com>\nSubject: SignalReader fails a whole round when goal-agent writes malformed JSON to signal.json\n\nBody:\nSignalReader fails a whole round when goal-agent writes malformed JSON to signal.json\r\n\r\n  Summary\r\n\r\n  When the goal-agent (Claude Code) writes <process_id>.signal.json at the end of a phase, refine's SignalReader waits 2000 ms for the file to become valid JSON. If parsing\r\n  still fails after the grace period, refine hard-fails the round with Workflow failed: Goal Agent completion signal �K remained invalid JSON. The round is dropped to\r\n  state=failed, phase=plan|implement, no source is touched, and no retry is attempted. Multiple unrelated goals are being burned this way �X the round agent worked fine, but\r\n  its terminal JSON payload had a structural mistake and there is no recovery path.\r\n\r\n  Blast radius (this box only, run/8082/)\r\n\r\n  - 7 distinct goal-agent sessions failed with this exact error pattern (grep signal.json remained invalid JSON in run/*/operations/*.json �� 7 hits).\r\n  - At least 3 distinct goals affected across recent runs:\r\n    - 00000SZWPPF3NJVZT6427CG00T �X \"PL LOB > Recent Claims > Claim Maintenance > Dates/Events > Select 'Accepted?'\"\r\n    - 00000SZW375SPJW874J5V7W005\r\n    - 00000SZW3ZX1PGY7E4TDV7W009\r\n  - Fails in both implementation_phase=plan (most common) and implement.\r\n\r\n  Failure signatures observed (all after 2000 ms)\r\n\r\n  �z�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�s�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�s�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�{\r\n  �x Column position �x                             Error                              �x       Session        �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2278 �x EOF while parsing an object                                    �x de381e6e             �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2296 �x EOF while parsing an object                                    �x db20f007             �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2449 �x EOF while parsing an object                                    �x 7648d691             �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2734 �x EOF while parsing an object                                    �x 137926a4 (this goal) �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2858 �x expected `,` or `}`                                            �x b6b61930             �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2932 �x EOF while parsing an object                                    �x 1543bdb8             �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 1 col 2958 �x expected `,` or `}`                                            �x 2dcbbb15             �x\r\n  �u�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�q�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�t\r\n  �x line 2 col 0    �x control character (\\u0000-\\u001F) found while parsing a string �x 60260633             �x\r\n  �|�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�r�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�r�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�w�}\r\n\r\n  All EOFs cluster at byte positions ~2.3�V3.0 KB. That is not a partial write footprint �X it is a fully written but structurally invalid JSON object, roughly the size the\r\n  completion-contract template implies once planning_result.summary/checklist are populated. The control character (\\u0000-\\u001F) variant is an unescaped newline embedded\r\n  inside a JSON string.\r\n\r\n  Root cause (code path)\r\n\r\n  src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs �X SignalReader::take:\r\n\r\n  let value = match serde_json::from_slice::<Value>(&bytes) {\r\n      Ok(value) => { ... }\r\n      Err(error) => {\r\n          let fingerprint = signal_fingerprint(&bytes);\r\n          // if fingerprint stable for SIGNAL_WRITE_GRACE_PERIOD (2s), hard-fail the round\r\n      }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  SIGNAL_WRITE_GRACE_PERIOD = Duration::from_secs(2) (agent_sessions.rs:24).\r\n\r\n  The 2-second byte-fingerprint mechanism is a proxy for \"the writer is still writing.\" It correctly handles a partial in-flight write. It does not distinguish \"the writer\r\n  is still going\" from \"the writer finished but produced invalid JSON.\" When Claude writes the signal in one shot (via the Write tool, atomically), the bytes are stable from\r\n  t=0, so the grace period elapses without change and the reader raises RefineError::InvalidInput, which propagates as the workflow failure.\r\n\r\n  Why the agent produces malformed JSON here\r\n\r\n  The completion-contract prompt for plan/criticize/revise (codec.rs:290+) asks the agent to write one inline JSON object whose planning_result field is a nested object with\r\n  a summary string and a checklist array of {id, description} items. In practice:\r\n\r\n  - Model produces long, multi-sentence summary / description values �� occasionally forgets to close a bracket at the tail (all 6 EOF failures land in the ~2.3�V3.0 KB range\r\n  where the closing braces would be).\r\n  - Model occasionally writes a raw newline inside a string in summary �� JSON parser hits the \\u0000-\\u001F guard.\r\n  - The prompt gives one long inline JSON example; there is no post-write validation step.\r\n\r\n  Nothing tells the agent it wrote invalid JSON. Nothing gives it a chance to correct it. Refine sees the malformed file, waits 2s, gives up.\r\n\r\n  Requested fix (in rough priority order)\r\n\r\n  1. Retry loop instead of hard-fail. On InvalidInput from SignalReader::take, don't kill the round. Feed the parse error back to the agent through the existing command\r\n  channel with a short \"your signal.json did not parse: <error> �X rewrite it, keeping the same shape\" prompt, and re-poll. Cap at N (e.g., 3) attempts before failing. This\r\n  alone would recover the majority of these failures.\r\n  2. Require atomic write in the contract. Change the completion-contract prompt to instruct the agent to write to signal.json.tmp then mv into place. Then SignalReader can\r\n  treat \"file exists\" as \"fully written\" and drop the fingerprint-grace hack �X a parse failure becomes immediately actionable (feeds into fix #1).\r\n  3. Shrink the wire format. The failure mode is \"long nested JSON written inline.\" Two lower-risk shapes:\r\n    - Split it: signal.json carries only {\"state\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}; planning_result.json (or implementation_evidence.json) is a separate artifact. A malformed\r\n  planning_result no longer nukes the state signal.\r\n    - Or accept JSONL: one top-level JSON value per line, so a truncated final line is skippable.\r\n  4. Preserve the bad bytes for diagnosis. Today, on InvalidInput, cleanup_session_artifacts removes the signal file (session_runtime.rs:210+). Copy it to\r\n  <process_id>.signal.invalid.json first so we can see what the agent actually wrote. Right now we're guessing from column offsets because the evidence is deleted.\r\n  5. Model-side self-check in the prompt. Add a line to the completion contract along the lines of \"after writing, verify the file parses (e.g., jq . <path>), and rewrite if\r\n  it does not.\" Cheap and stacks with the other fixes.\r\n\r\n  Repro / evidence pointers\r\n\r\n  - Grace-period source: src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs:199�V254, agent_sessions.rs:24\r\n  - Prompt template that shapes the output: src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs:290�V (completion_contract)\r\n  - Recent operation files with the error: run/8082/operations/1a00549*, 1a005b87*, 1a005c81*, 1a005c85*, 1a005ca9*, 1a005d3b*, 1a005e40*\r\n  - Cleanup that deletes the offending bytes: src/process/agent_sessions/codec.rs:265�V273, called from session_runtime.rs:210, 224, 236\r\n\r\n\r\n[cid:insurity-small2_2f81c33c-d951-4e5c-a467-1113541ca22c.jpg]\r\nBuddy Williams\r\nBuddy.Williams@insurity.com\r\n\r\n[cid:excellence2026signature(17b0688e-5473-4b74-96eb-a73f633f2c2f)_48407359-d77b-4967-95cd-277a32b50ebc.png]<https://insurity.com/excellence?utm_source=Email-Signature&utm_medium=Email&utm_campaign=Event-Excellence-2026>\r\n\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe information contained in this e-mail message is intended only for the personal and confidential use of the intended recipient(s). This message may be an attorney-client communication 